{"generated_at": "2026-10-18T18:17:25.048900+00:00", "slug": "issue-maternal-health-live", "title": "Maternal health and doulas, 18 days of posts", "stats": {"posts_processed": 7, "claims": 13, "clusters": 12, "checkable": 11, "verified": 2, "unsupported_spreading": 0, "cross_platform": 1, "news_checked": 0, "crossed_over": 0}, "clusters": [{"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": null, "id": 1, "text": "Texas health officials are delaying release of the state's maternal death report until after the midterm elections.", "type": "fact", "checkable": true, "stance": "against", "entities": ["Texas", "Texas Health and Human Services Commission", "Texas Department of State Health Services"], "verdict": "supported", "verdict_basis": "DSHS moved the 2026 joint report of the Maternal Mortality and Morbidity Review Committee from its usual Sept. 1 date to Dec. 1. That is after the Nov. 3 election. \nKXAN reported that DSHS changed the date from Sept. 1 to Dec. 1\n. The Texas Tribune reported that \nthe state is permitting the delay under a 2025 law that gives agencies more leeway on report submissions\n. The Tribune also noted that \nthis is the second time since 2013 that the review has come out after a midterm election, the last being 2022\n. DSHS says the report \n\"isn't delayed\"\n. It says the acting commissioner asked the committee to strengthen the report, and that HB 4666 sets a Dec. 1 deadline. \nThe Amarillo Tribune reported that the report could still be published earlier\n. Political motive is alleged by Democratic lawmakers and advocates, and DSHS disputes it. The claim as worded is about timing, not motive, and the timing is documented. The only qualification is that DSHS disputes the word \"delay\" and the election-related intent that the wording can imply.", "verdict_sources": ["https://www.texastribune.org/2026/09/25/texas-maternal-mortality-committee-report-election-delay/", "https://www.ktsm.com/news/release-of-2026-maternal-mortality-report-pushed-back-3-months/", "https://www.houstonpublicmedia.org/articles/news/health-science/2026/09/15/561866/texas-maternal-death-report-abortion-midterm-election/", "https://amarillotribune.org/2026/09/22/texass-biannual-maternal-death-report-yet-to-be-released-heres-what-we-do-know/", "https://www.texasobserver.org/texas-maternal-mortality-report-delay-elections-dshs/"], "posts": 2, "views": 671437, "accounts": 2, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "report_delay_coverup", "label": "Mortality report delay is cover-up", "color": "#d95926", "posts": 2}], "first_seen": "2026-10-03T01:57:00+00:00", "first_handle": "LunaForTruth", "first_handles": ["LunaForTruth", "marytuma.bsky.social"], "first_url": "https://x.com/LunaForTruth/status/2106201821358493969", "first_source": "x", "first_name": "Luna 🇺🇸", "sources": {"x": {"posts": 1, "views": 671437, "engagement": 7611, "first_seen": "2026-10-03T01:57:00+00:00", "first_handle": "LunaForTruth", "first_url": "https://x.com/LunaForTruth/status/2106201821358493969"}, "bsky": {"posts": 1, "views": 0, "engagement": 184, "first_seen": "2026-10-07T15:49:03.044000+00:00", "first_handle": "marytuma.bsky.social", "first_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/marytuma.bsky.social/post/3mxccayrmgc2w"}}, "cross_platform": true, "platform_lag_h": 109.9, "first_views": 671437, "last_seen": "2026-10-07T15:49:03.044000+00:00", "views_24h": 0, "series": [["2026-10-03T01:57:00+00:00", 671437], ["2026-10-07T15:49:03.044000+00:00", 0]], "top_post": "https://x.com/LunaForTruth/status/2106201821358493969"}, {"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": null, "id": 2, "text": "Ectopic pregnancy deaths rose faster in states with abortion bans than in other states.", "type": "fact", "checkable": true, "stance": "against", "entities": [], "verdict": "supported", "verdict_basis": "ProPublica analyzed CDC WONDER data. It found that \nectopic deaths rose nationwide, but the climb was much steeper in states that banned abortion after Roe was overturned\n. F